  "summary": "The code suffered from critical performance bottlenecks due to redundant sorting and potential runtime crashes from missing key/index checks. The refactored version optimizes the leader lookup to O(N) per snapshot and adds robust error handling and type safety.",
  "fixed_code": "from typing import List, Dict, Any\n\ndef leaderboard_snapshots(users: List[Dict[str, Any]], snapshots: List[Any]) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Returns a list of leaderboard leaders for each given snapshot timestamp.\"\"\"\n    if not users:\n        return [{'at': snap, 'leader': None} for snap in snapshots]\n\n    results = []\n    for snap in snapshots:\n        # O(M) lookup instead of O(M log M) sort\n        leader = max(users, key=lambda u: u.get('score', 0))\n        results.append({'at': snap, 'leader': leader.get('name')})\n    return results"
